$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Library Procedure To a stirred
suspension of the input phenol (3, 1.2 g, 3.71 mmol), polymer-supported
triphenylphosphine (3.7 g, 11.1 mmol) and the alcohol (5.6 mmol) in
dichloromethane (100 mL) was added a solution of
di-tert-butylazodicarboxylate (DTAD) (2.14 g, 9.3 mmol) in
dichloromethane (10 mL) at 0 °C over a period of 1 hour. The resulting
suspension was lightly agitated for 16 hours at room temperature and the
resin was removed by filtration and the filtrate was concentrated to
dryness to afford 7. Yield 100%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reagent, Mitsunobu reaction
