$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1-Phenyl-5-(2-propynylthio)-1H-tetrazole [12].
Following the General Procedure, 1-phenyl- 1H-tetrazole-5-thiol, 11, (404
mg, 2.27 mmol) was coupled to propargyl alcohol (120 µL, 2.06 mmol) using
3 (871 mg, 2.37 mmol) and triphenylphosphine (594 mg, 2.26 mmol).
Filtration of the reaction mixture afforded the reduced azodicarboxylate
4 as a white powder (677 mg, 77 mol % recovery). Flash chromatography
eluted with 1:19 EtOAc/hexanes to 1:14 EtOAc/hexanes afforded the title
compound as a white powder (444 mg, quantitative yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
