$DATUM 1S)-[2-(5-Bromo-pyridin-3-yloxy)-1-hydroxymethyl-ethyl]- carbamic Acid
tert-Butyl Ester (17). A 100 mL RBF was charged with
3-bromo-5-hydroxypyridine (8, 1.20 g, 6.87 mmol),20 (R)-[1-
(tert-butyl-dimethyl-silanyloxymethyl)-2-hydroxy-ethyl]-carbamic acid
tert-butyl ester (16, 2.1 g, 6.87 mmol),18 and Ph3P (2.34 g, 8.93 mmol)
and was purged with N2. THF (30 mL) was added at 0 °C. After stirring at
0 °C for 10 min, diethyl azodicarboxylate (DEAD, 1.41 mL, 8.93 mmol) was
added via syringe. The reaction mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 0.5 h and
at rt for 2 h. The reaction mixture was concentrated, and the residue was
separated by flash chromatography (5-25% gradient EtOAc in hexane) to
provide the coupled product (3.14 g, 99%).
