$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a stirred solution of 15b (24.0 mg, 44.2 μmol) in pyridine (3 mL) was
added acetic anhydride (0.1 mL, 0.90 mmol). After stirring for 36 h at 50
°C, the reaction mixture was concentrated. The residue was purified by
column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc, 1:2) to give 15ba (27.1 mg, 43.3
μmol, 98% yield) as a colorless oil. [α]D20 +10.0 (c 1.0, CHCl3). 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3): 1.11 (3H, s), 1.12 (3H, s), 1.14 (6H, s), 1.19 (3H, s),
1.20 (3H, s), 1.20 (3H, s), 1.22 (1H, m), 1.32-1.72 (6H, m), 1.80-1.99
(8H, m), 2.00-2.07, (5H, m), 2.04 (3H, s), 2.08 (3H, s), 3.05 (1H, d, J
=9.3 Hz), 3.23 (1H, dd, J = 2.2, 11.3 Hz), 3.71 (1H, t, J = 6.9 Hz), 3.77
(1H, dd, J = 6.2, 8.8 Hz), 4.94 (1H, brs), 4.95, (1H, dd, J = 2.2, 10.0
Hz), 5.06 (1H, brs), 5.22 (1H, t, J = 6.7 Hz). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3):
20.08 (q), 21.17 (q), 21.29 (q), 22.77 (q), 23.16 (q), 24.01 (q), 24.41
(t), 25.15 (t), 26.13 (t), 26.62 (t), 27.29 (t), 27.44 (q), 27.64 (t),
29.730 (t), 34.65 (t), 34.93 (t), 39.83 (t), 69.61 (s), 70.46 (s), 70.55
(s), 76.61 (d), 77.15 (d), 83.81 (d), 83.94 (s), 83.99 (d), 84.12 (s),
86.93 (d), 87.05 (d), 112.16 (t), 146.29 (s), 170.48 (s), 171.05 (s).
CIMS m/z 627 [M+ H]+ (3), 609 (40), 549 (100). HRCIMS calcd 627.4108 for
C34H59O10, found 627.4096 [M+ H]+. IR (neat, cm-1): 3453, 1734.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
