$DATUM p-Methoxyphenyl Ether (7). To a solution of the benzyl alcohol 63 (40 mg,
97 μmol) in benzene (3 mL) were successively added Ph3P (50 mg, 0.19
mmol), p-methoxyphenol (24 mg, 0.19 mmol), and DEAD (40% toluene
solution, 86 μL, 0.19 mol) at room temperature. The reaction mixture was
stirred for 15 min and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude
product was purified by preparative TLC (hexane/ EtOAc, 3:2) to afford
the p-methoxyphenyl ether 7 (48 mg, 96%) as a colorless oil. 7, yield (48
mg, 96%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.42- 7.35 (m, 5H), 6.89-6.77 (m,
4H), 6.74 (s, 1H), 6.54 (s, 1H), 5.12 (d, J = 11.4 Hz, 1H), 5.05 (d, J =
11.4 Hz, 1H), 4.93 (s, 2H), 4.32 (dd, J = 5.8, 11.5 Hz, 1H), 3.96 (d, J =
15.6 Hz, 1H), 3.91 (t, J = 11.2 Hz, 1H), 3.77 (s, 3H), 3.50 (dd, J = 5.1,
15.1 Hz, 1H), 3.35 (dd, J = 5.8, 11.0 Hz, 1H), 3.22 (t, J = 5.1 Hz, 1H),
3.06 (d, J = 3.7 Hz, 1H), 1.59 (s, 3H), 1.50 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 157.2, 154.1, 152.6, 147.1, 138.3, 136.2, 128.8, 128.3, 127.5,
115.8, 114.7, 113.0, 111.2, 105.6, 99.9, 93.1,70.3, 59.3, 55.7, 54.8,
51.5, 49.8, 32.6, 30.1, 24.3; IR (neat) 1585, 1507, 1228, 1120 cm-1;
[α]23 D -24.2 (c 0.39, CHCl3); HRMS (EI) m/z calcd for C30H31NO7 ([M]+)
517.2101, found 517.2145.
