$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for polyglycerol supported
Mitsunobu reactions This reaction was carried out under an inert gas
atmosphere and exclusion of water. In a 50 mL-Schlenk-tube with magnetic
stirrer the acidic component (0.5 mmol, 1 eq.), the alcohol (2 mmol, 4
eq. if easily removable, otherwise 0.5 mmol, 1 eq.), and
p-(diphenylphosphino)benzoic acid polyglycerylester 10 (0.481 g, 2.60
mmol PPh3 g-1, 1.25 mmol, 2 eq.) were dissolved in abs. THF (5 mL). Under
stirring, a solution of azodicarboxylic acid ethyl polyglyceryl ester 6
(0.500 g, 2.50 mmol azo groups g-1, 1.25 mmol, 2 eq.) in abs. THF (5 mL)
was added dropwise. Immediately precipitation occured. The mixture was
stirred at ambient temperature and the conversion was followed by means
of TLC. When the reaction had finished, the mixture was filtered and to
the filtrate was added little by little freshly distilled diethylether
(80 mL). The precipitated polymer was separated via filtration over
Celite. The filtrate was concentrated in vacuo and tested on residual
polymer traces by means of TLC. If necessary an additional
precipitation/filtration step was attached. In some cases a filtration
over silica gel was necessary to remove the polymer traces completely.
Benzylphenylether. Conversion according 1H-NMR: 51%. 1H-NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3; sample contains substrate at δ=7.49-6.76, 5.17): δ=7.49-6.76
(Ar-H), 5.06 (Bn-H); 13C-NMR (COSY, CDCl3): δ= 158.4 (1-C), 136.9 (8-C),
130.0 (3-C/5-C), 128.3 (10-C/12-C), 127.8 (11-C), 126.4 (9- C/13-C),
121.5 (4-C), 115.4 (2-C/6-C), 70.1 (7-C); GC-MS (EI): m/z(%) = 184.0 (10)
[M], 91.0 (100) [Bn], 65.0 (20) [C5H6].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 51% conversion
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM High-loading polyglycerol supported reagents for Mitsunobu and acylation
reactions and other useful polyglycerol derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Roller, Sebastian; Zhou, Haixia; Haag, Rainer
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
