$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Mitsunobu Reaction of amino alcohols with 2-bromophenol: The amino
alcohol (1.0 equiv.) was dissolved in Benzene (0.1M) with the 2-
bromophenol (1.5 equiv.) and triphenylphosphine (1.5 equiv.). Solid
1,1'-Azodicarbonyldipiperidine (1.5 equiv.) was then added and the
reaction mixture stirred for 12h, then diluted with EtOAc and washed with
1M NaOH (x 2) and brine (x 1). The EtOAc layer was then dried over K2CO3
and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue thus obtained was
chromatographed over SiO2 to yield the aminoether.
(1R,2S)-Dimethyl-[1-methyl-2-(2-bromophenoxy)-2-phenylethyl]-amine.
Colorless oil. Yield: 92%. Rf = 0.33 (TEA-washed SiO2, Hexanes/EtOAc/TEA
: 66:33:1). Rf = 0.33 IR (film/cm-1): 1476s, 1276s, 1245s, 1030m, 995m,
744s, 700m. δH (500MHz, CDCl3): 1.24 (d, J7.5Hz, 3H, -CHCH3), 2.41 (s,
6H, -NCH3), 2.96 (m, 1H, - NCHCH3), 5.44 (d, J2.5Hz, 1H, -OCHPh), 6.58
(dd, J8.5Hz, 1.5Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 6.73 (m, 1H, Ar-H), 7.03 (m, 1H, Ar-H),
7.22-7.33 (m, 5H, Ar-H), 7.52 (dd, 1H, J8Hz, 1.5Hz, 1H, Ar-H). δc
(125MHz, CDCl3): 8.1 (-CHCH3), 41.7 (-NCH3), 65.9 (-NCHCH3), 80.1
(-OCHPh), 112.5, 114.2, 121.5, 126.0, 127.4, 128.2, 128.5, 133.3, 140.0,
153.6. HRMS found 334.0808. C17H21BrNO (MH+) requires 334.0806. [α]D
(23°C) = -120.5 (c = 2.33, CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mitsunobu reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Syntheses of stereochemically diverse nine-membered ring-containing
biaryls
