(GP2) The secondary alcohol (1.0 equiv), the phenol (1.2 equiv) and PPh3
(1.2 equiv) were dissolved in THF (c = 0.1-0.2 M). After addition of
DEAD/DIAD (1.4 equiv) the reaction was stirred until conversion was
complete (40 °C, 3-6 h). Subsequently, the solvent was removed in vacuo
and the residue was directly purified by FCC. 2-O-[4'
-(5''-Methyl-[1,2,4]oxadiazol-3''yl)-phenyl]-5-O-[4'''-(2''''-methylsulfonylphenyl)-phenyl]-1,4:3,6-dianhydro-D-sorbitole
(55); Typical Procedure. Following GP2, 54 (564 mg, 1.50 mmol) was
treated with 46 (317 mg, 1.80 mmol),37 PPh3 (472 mg, 1.80 mmol, 1.2
equiv) and DIAD (0.41 mL, 2.08 mmol). FCC purification (pentane-MTBE, 1:1
→ 1:2 → MTBE) provided 55 (740 mg, 1.38 mmol, 92%) as a colorless solid.
Mp 55 °C (MTBE); Rf = 0.32 (MTBE) [α]589 = 64, [α]578 = 67, [α]546 = 76,
[α]436 = 131, [α]365 = 207 (c = 1.014, CHCl3, 19 °C). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 2.61 (s, 3 H), 2.62 (s, 3 H), 4.04 (dd, J = 9.8, 5.4 Hz, 1
H), 4.07-4.16 (m, 2 H), 4.25 (dd, J = 10.5, 3.9 Hz, 1 H), 4.69 (d, J =
4.9 Hz, 1 H), 4.86 (q, J = 5.5 Hz, 1 H), 4.91 (d, J = 3.2 Hz, 1 H), 5.03
(t, J = 5.0 Hz, 1 H), 6.99-7.05 (m, 4 H), 7.34 (dd, J = 7.5, 1.3 Hz, 1
H), 7.40 (pd, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 H), 7.51 (td, J = 7.7, 1.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.61
(td, J = 7.5, 1.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.99 (pd, J = 9.0 Hz, 2 H), 8.20 (dd, J =
7.9, 1.3 Hz, 1 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 12.3, 43.1, 71.1, 73.5,
77.7, 81.3, 81.7, 86.2, 114.7, 115.4, 120.1, 127.7, 128.2, 132.8, 133.0,
129.1, 131.36, 131.43, 139.4, 140.9, 158.0, 159.1, 167.8, 176.2. HRMS
(ESI): m/z [M + Na+] calcd for C28H26N2NaO7S: 557.1358; found: 557.1382.
