$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(8S)-8-(2-Fluorophenyl)-N,N,2,3-tetramethyl-3,6,7,8-tetrahy- General
Procedure 10 (Mitsunobu Cyclization to Tetrahydrochromenoimidazoles).
Asolution of the corresponding diol and triphenylphosphine (1.3 to 3.0
equiv) in tetrahydrofuran was treated with DIAD (1.3 to 3.0 equiv), and
the mixture was stirred for 5 min to 18 h at room temperature.
(8S)-8-(2-Chloro-4-fluorophenyl)-N,N,2,3-tetramethyl-3,6,7,
8-tetrahydrochromeno[7,8-d]imidazole-5-carboxamide (116). The title
compound was prepared by Mitsunobu cyclization of diol 99 (16.5 g, 39
mmol) as described in general procedure 10 (reaction time: 0.5 h).
Workup: The reaction mixture was diluted with water and a pH value of 3
was adjusted by addition of 2 N hydrochloric acid (40 mL). The acidic
solution was extracted with ethyl acetate (3x), and the organic extracts
were discarded. The aqueous phase was treated with concentrated ammonia
solution (20 mL) until a pH value of 9.5 was obtained. A precipitate was
formed which was collected by filtration, washed with water, and dried in
vacuo at temperatures of 50 and 100 °C. This afforded the pure title
compound in 91% yield (14.4 g of a colorless solid). 1HNMR (DMSO-d6, 300
MHz): δ =1.99 (mc, 1 H), 2.28 (mc, 1 H), 2.48 (s, 3 H), 2.63 (mc, 1 H),
2.80, 2.87 (s,mc, 4 H), 3.01 (s, 3 H), 3.68 (s, 3 H), 5.43 (dd, 1 H),
6.96 (s, 1 H), 7.34 (mc, 1 H), 7.53 (mc, 1 H), 7.66 (mc, 1 H). HRMS calcd
for C21H22ClFN3O2 m/z (MH+), 402.1379; found, 402.1379.
