$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Benzothiazole Sulfides 3; General Procedure.
To a solution of 2-mercaptobenzothiazole (2; 1.10 equiv), Ph3P (1.10
equiv), and the corresponding alcohol 1 (0.279-2.84 mmol, 1.00 equiv) in
anhyd THF (14.5 mL/mmol 1) was added DIAD (1.10 equiv) dropwise. The
reaction mixture was stirred for 15 h atr.t. The solvent was removed
under reduced pressure and the resulting yellow residue was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel (cHex-EtOAc) to afford the title
compounds 3. 2-[2-(Trifluoromethyl)benzylthio]benzo[d]thiazole as a
colorless oil, yield 0.832 g, 2.56 mmol, 90%. Rf = 0.59 (cHex-EtOAc,
10:1). IR (KBr): 3065, 1943, 1607, 1584, 1497, 1459, 1428, 1316, 1240,
1179 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 4.84 (s, 2 H, CH2), 7.32 (ddd, J
= 1.2, 7.4, 8.3 Hz, 1 H, ArH-4'), 7.37 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 1 H, ArH-6), 7.44
(ddd, J = 1.2, 7.4, 8.3 Hz, 1 H, ArH-3'), 7.49 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1 H,
ArH-5), 7.68 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1 H, ArH-4), 7.75 (d, J = 2.9 Hz, 1 H,
ArH-7), 7.74-7.78 (m, 1 H, ArH-5'), 7.92 (m, 1 H, ArH-6'). 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 33.7, 121.1, 121.6, 122.9, 124.4, 126.1, 126.2, 127.8,
128.6, 128.9, 131.8, 132.3, 135.4, 153.0, 166.0.19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3):
δ = -59.3. MS (70 eV, EI): m/z (%) = 325 (96, [M+]), 159 (100,
[C8H6F3+]), 109 (36). HR-EIMS: m/z calcd for C15H10F3NS2: 325.0206;
found: 325.0209. Anal. Calcd for C15H10F3NS2: C, 55.37; H, 3.10; N, 4.30;
S, 19.71. Found: C, 55.43; H, 3.23; N, 4.45; S, 19.31.
