$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Mitsunobu Cyclodehydration Reaction;
1-(Trifluoromethyl)-1,3-dihydroisobenzofuran (2d) ; Typical Procedure To
a stirred solution of the fluorinated diol 1d (49.4 mg, 0.24 mmol) in
anhyd benzene (2.5 mL) was added Bu4P (0.12 mL, 0.48 mmol) followed by
TMAD (95 mg, 0.55 mmol) at r.t. The reaction mixture was then flushed
with argon, sealed, and allowed to stir for 12 h at the same temperature.
The crude mixture was then purified by flash column chromatography
(silica gel 60-230 mesh, 10:1 mixture of pentane and CH2Cl2 as eluent).
1-Phenyl-1-(trifluoromethyl)isochroman (2k) 1H NMR: δ = 7.57-7.46 (m, 3
H), 7.39-7.25 (m, 5 H), 7.24-7.19 (m, 1 H), 4.09 (ddd, J = 3.3, 5.7, 11.1
Hz, 1 H), 3.76 (dt, J = 3.9, 10.8 Hz, 1 H), 3.12 (ddd, J = 5.8, 10.2,
16.1 Hz, 1 H), 2.67 (dt, J = 3.6, 16.4 Hz, 1 H). 13C NMR: δ = 137.59,
135.13, 131.30, 129.62, 128.88, 128.65, 128.27, 127.90 (q, 3 J C,F = 3.4
Hz), 125.99, 125.22 (q, 1 J C,F = 286.2 Hz), 80.96 (q, 2 J C,F = 27.9
Hz), 60.93, 28.58. 19F NMR: δ = -73.71. HRMS (EI): m/z calcd for
C16H13F3O: 278.0918; found: 278.0916.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mitsunobu reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cyclodehydration of fluorinated diols using the Mitsunobu reaction:
highly efficient synthesis of trifluoromethylated cyclic ethers
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Prakash, G. K. Surya; Do, Clement; Wang, Fang; Mathew, Thomas; Olah,
George A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2010), (11), 1891-1898

