$DATUM ii. Double Mitsunobu reaction: Diol (13) (153.9 mg, 0.172 mmol) was
dissolved in anhydrous benzene (10 mL) with 2-Bromophenol (80 μL, 0.688
mmol, 4.0 equiv.) and triphenylphosphine (180.5 mg, 0.688 mmol, 4.0
equiv.). Solid 1,1'-Azodicarbonyl dipiperidine (173.6 mg, 0.688 mmol, 4.0
equiv.) was added and the reaction mixture stirred for 12 h, then diluted
with EtOAc (40 mL) and washed with 1M NaOH (20 mL x 2) and brine (1 x 20
mL). The EtOAc layer was then dried over K2CO3 and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue thus obtained was chromatographed over SiO2
(TEA-washed, Hexanes/EtOAc/TEA : 95:5:1) to yield the diamine (14) as a
colorless oil, 186.5 mg (90% yield). Rf, 0.33 TEA-washed SiO2,
Hexanes/EtOAc/TEA : 95:5:1). 14, 186.5 mg (90% yield). Rf, 0.33 IR
(film)/cm-1: 2940s, 1475s, 1244s, 745s. δH (500MHz, CDCl3): 0.98 (m, 21H,
C(9)H and C(10)H3), 1.25 (m, 2H, C(6)H2), 1.29 (d, J7Hz, 3H, C(3)H3),
1.31 (d, J7Hz, 3H, C(3')H3), 1.39-1.48 (m, 3H, C(6')H2 and C(7)H),
2.48-2.60 (m, 2H, C(5)H2 or C(5')H2), 2.63-2.71 (m, 2H, C(5)H2 or
C(5')H2), 3.07 (m, 2H, C(2)H and C(2')H), 3.40 (m, 2H, C(8)H2), 3.82
(ABq, JAB15.5Hz, 2H, C(4)H2), 3.83 (ABq, JAB16.5Hz, 2H, C(4')H2), 5.31
(d, J7Hz, 1H, C(1)H), 5.32 (d, J7Hz, 1H, C(1')H), 6.58 (app. dd, J8.5Hz,
1Hz, 2H, Ar-H), 6.70 (m, 2H, Ar-H), 6.99 (m, 4H, Ar-H), 7.08 (m, 2H,
Ar-H), 7.18-7.25 (m, 13H, Ar-H), 7.46 (m, 3H, Ar-H).δc (125MHz, CDCl3):
10.0, 10.2, 12.0, 18.2, 30.5, 37.3, 48.5, 48.9, 54.82, 54.87, 61.56,
61.62, 65.6, 81.4, 81.6, 112.43, 112.45, 114.2, 121.48, 121.50, 123.79,
123.83, 126.43, 126.48, 127.2, 127.4, 127.86, 127.89, 128.2, 130.25,
130.29, 132.32, 132.34, 133.3, 139.8, 140.1, 140.15, 153.92, 153.96. m/z
(ESI): 603 (1/2 x MH2 2+ :100%).
