$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 18 A magnetically stirred solution of bromohydrin 174 (1.50 g,
4.57 mmol) in methanol (30 mL) was treated with sodium methoxide (740 mg,
13.7 mmol) and the resulting solution stirred at 18 °C for 14 h then
concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue thus obtained was
dissolved ethyl acetate (100 mL) and the ensuing solution washed with
NH4Cl (1 × 30 ml of a saturated aqueous solution). The separated organic
layer was dried (Na2SO4) then filtered and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The resulting light-yellow oil was subjected to flash
chromatography (silica, 1:2 v/v ethyl acetate/hexane elution) and
concentration of the appropriate fractions (Rf = 0.3 in 1:1 v/v ethyl
acetate/hexane) then afforded alcohol 18 Clear, colorless oil(1.15 g,
90%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.19 (d, J = 1.8 Hz, 1H), 4.60 (dd, J =
5.2 and 1.8 Hz, 1H), 4.53 (dd, J = 5.0 and 2.5 Hz, 1H), 3.96 (m, 1H),
3.79 (dd, J = 8.2 and 2.5 Hz, 1H), 3.49 (s, 3H), 2.75 (broad s, 1H), 1.42
(s, 3H), 1.41 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 129.1, 123.6, 110.8,
78.9, 78.1, 76.3, 71.2, 57.5, 27.3, 26.3. IR (KBr): νmax 3439, 2985,
2917, 1641, 1577, 1540, 1383, 1233, 1218, 1158, 1097, 1061, 1043, 997
cm-1. MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z 265 and 263 [(M-Me.P+ both 40%], 193 (66), 191
(73), 180 and 178 (both 30), 124 (60), 101 (100). HRMS [(M-Me.)+ Calcd
for C9H12 81BrO4: 264.9898. Found: 264.9897. Calcd for C9H12 79BrO4:
262.9919. Found: 262.9910. Specific rotation [α]D20 = -89.9 (c 1.5,
CHCl3)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chemoenzymatic Total Synthesis and Reassignment of the Absolute
Configuration of Ribisin C
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lan, Ping; Banwell, Martin G.; Ward, Jas S.; Willis, Anthony C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(1), 228-231

