$DATUM Synthesis of thioethers 2a-c 1.00 g (1.4 mmol) thiacalix[4]arene 1 and
1.46 g (5.6 mmol) TPP were dissolved in THF (30 mL) and appropriate
thioalkyl alcohol (13.9 mmol) was added. After that, 0.87mL (5.6 mmol)
DEAD was added dropwise at -10 °C and stirred at r.t. for 1 day; and
then, heated to 40-50 °C and stirred for 16 h. After completion of
reaction, THF was removed under reduced pressure and methanol was added
to residue, precipitate was filtered and dried in vacuum. Compound 2a:
white powder. Mp 182-185 °C (decomp.), R f (Hex:EtOAc = 4:1) = 0.63, R f
(diethyl ether:petroleum ether = 1:8) = 0.32. anal. calcd. for
C46H60O4S6*2C5H12: C 66.35, H 8.35; found: C 66.36, H 8.15. m/z (p-NA)
891.9 [M+Na]+, 909.8 [M+K]+. 1H NMR (Bruker AVANCE-600, CDCl3, 303K) 7.84
(s, 2H, OH), 7.68 (s, 4H, Harom), 6.96 (s, 4H, Harom), 4.66 (t, 3 J HH =
7.3 Hz, 4H, OCH2), 3.15 (t, 3 J HH = 7.1 Hz, 4H, CH2S), 2.26 (s, 6H,
CH3), 1.34 (s, 18H, t-Bu), 0.80 (s, 18H, t-Bu).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative solvent toluene gave lower yield, Mitsunobu reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Characterization of Thiacalix[4]monocrowns Modified by
Thioether Groups on the Lower Rim
