$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A mixture of
2-chloro-4-cyclohexyloxybenzaldehyde (1.0 g, 4.19 mmol),
2,4-thiazolidinedione (490 mg, 4.19 mmol), piperidine (0.21 ml, 2.1 mmol)
and acetic acid (0.14 ml, 2.1 mmol) in toluene (20 ml) was then added to
a round bottom flask fitted with a Dean-Stark water trap and stirred
under reflux for overnight. After cooling to room temperature, the
precipitate was washed with hexane. Compound was obtained by
recrystallization. Intermediate of
5-(4-(Benzyloxy)-2-chlorobenzylidene)thiazolidine-2,4-dione (6), Yield:
89%.
