$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
5-(2-Chloro-4-(cyclohexyloxy)benzylidene)thiazolidine-2,4-dione (1). To a
stirring solution of cyclohexanol (1.0 g, 10 mmol),
2-chloro-4-hydroxybenzaldehyde (1.54 g, 10 mmol) and triphenylphosphine
(2.62 g, 10 mmol) in THF (20 ml) was slowly added diethyl
azodicarboxylate (40 % in toluene, 3.35 g, 10 mmol) over 10 min. at 0 °C.
The mixture was then stirred at room temperature until the disappearance
of starting materials (TLC analysis). The resulting solution was
concentrated under reduced pressure and purified by column chromatography
over silica gel (elution with hexane/ethyl acetate, 20:1). Intermediate
of 5-(2-Chloro-3-(4-cyclohexylbutoxy)benzylidene)thiazolidine-2,4-dione
(14), Yield: 89%.
