$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-(2-Pyridinylmethoxy)phenol. An oven dried flask charged with resorcinol
monobenzoate (2.14 g, 10.0 mmol) and PPh3 (3.32 g, 12.7 mmol) was purged
with N2 and immersed in an ambient temperature water bath. After the
addition of dry THF (30 mL) and 2-hydroxymethylpyridine (1.16 mL, 11.0
mmol), diisopropyl azodicarboxylate (2.17 mL, 11.0 mmol) was added to the
stirred solution over 5 min and the flask was left at ambient temperature
for 4 h. Volatiles were removed under reduced pressure to give a brown
oil to which was added 30% Et2O/light petroleum (bp 40-60 °C) and the
mixture was stirred rapidly for 30 min. Filtration, and concentration of
the supernatant liquid to afforded compound. 3-Alkoxyphenyl Benzoate
Derivative, Yield: 88%, light brown oil.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mitsunobu reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
