$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the epoxide synthesis (Scheme S-2) In a
round-bottomed flask the desired diol and phosphine were disolved in
anhydrous CH2Cl2 at room temperature. Next, neat DIAD was added dropwise
(5-10 seconds) and the reaction progress was followed by TLC. Once the
reaction finished, the solvent was removed under vacuum and the crude
purified by column chromatography (on SiO2/NEt3 2.5%, hexane as eluent).
2,3,3-triphenyloxirane (2a)4 Prepared according to general procedure from
a solution of (S)-1,1,2-triphenylethane- 1,2-diol 1a (50 mg, 0.172 mmols,
1 eq), phosphine (0.181 mmols, 1.05 eq), anhydrous CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL) and
DIAD (36 μL, 0.181 mmols, 1.05 eq). A white solid or colorless oil is
obtained (depending on which is the enantiomeric purity) after
purification. Yields and ee's, depending on the phosphine used, are shown
in the article. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.33 (s, 1H), 7.02-7.05 (m,
2H), 7.13-7.16 (m, 3H), 7.20 (s, 5H), 7.27-7.39 (m, 5H) ppm; HPLC Daicel
CHIRALCEL-ODR. MeOH 100%, 0.5 mL/min, λ = 254 nm, tR (S) = 10.7 min, tR
(R) = 17.3 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mitsunobu cyclodeyhydration
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phosphine-Dependent Stereoselectivity in the Mitsunobu Cyclodehydration
