$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A suspension of 2-acetamido-2-deoxy-a-D-glucopyranose[29] (20.52 g, 92.8
mmol) and dry Amber-Iite IR-120 (H+ form) resin (20.5 g) in dry methanol
(600 mL) was refluxed for 14 hr. The resin was removed, and washed with
methanol (3 x 60 mL). The combined solutions were concentrated to give a
solid residue of methyl 2-acetamido-2-deoxy-α-D-glucopyranoside (19.00 g,
87%). From 13C NMR spectral peak heights, this product was an
approximately 6:1 ratio of α to β products. 13C NMR (D2O) δ: 100.9 (C β
-1), 100.3 (C α -1), 74.4 (C α -5), 73.9 (C α -3), 72.8 (C α -4), 63.4 (C
α -6), 57.9 (OCH3), 56.4 (C α -2), 24.7 (COCH3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, /β 6:1, amberlite IR-120 (H+) used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An Efficient Synthesis of Derivatives of
2-Acetamido-4-amino-2,4,6-trideoxy-D-galactopyranose
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Liang, Hong; Grindley, T. Bruce
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Carbohydrate Chemistry (2004), 23(2 & 3), 71-82

