$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3.4 General procedure for the preparation of monofunctionalised
pentabromobenzene (2) To an ice-cooled solution of triphenylphosphine
(100 mmol) in dry THF was added diisopropylazodicarboxylate (Aldrich #
22554-1, 100 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at RT for 10 minutes
before alkyl alcohol (100 mmol) and pentabromophenol (100 mmol) were
added. The ice-bath was removed and the reaction mixture was stirred
overnight at RT. The product was obtained by usual workup in 40-80%
overall yield. Finally, product was purified by the column chromatography
eluting hexane-ethyl acetate (EtOAc) (100:10). The analytical data are
reported elsewhere (28).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mitsunobu reaction conditions used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Room temperature columnar phase: Influence of 2-ethylhexane peripheral
chain on the mesomorphism of polyalkynylbenzene-based disc-shaped
molecules
