$DATUM 3' ' ',4' ' '-Anhydro-1,3,2',6',2' ' ',6' '
'-hexa-N-(tert-butoxycarbonyl)- 5' '-deoxy-5' '-(4-nitrobenzoyl)-neomycin
B (5). DIAD (330 µL, 1.65 mmol) was added slowly to a cold solution of 2
(200 mg, 0.165 mmol), TPP (430 mg, 1.65 mmol), and 4-nitrobenzoic acid
(330 mg, 2.0 mmol) in dry solvent (2 mL toluene + 1 mL THF) under a dry
N2 atmosphere. The mixture was stirred at room temperature (18 h) and
then evaporated to dryness. Column chromatography on silica (DCM/MeOH
97:3 → 95:5) afforded 5 (187 mg, 85%) as a white amorphous solids. HRMS
(ESI): calculated for (M + Na+) C60H95N7O27 1368.61736, found 1368.61214.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Multi-site Modification of Neomycin B: Combined Mitsunobu and Click
Chemistry Approach
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Quader, Sabina; Boyd, Sue E.; Jenkins, Ian D.; Houston, Todd A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2007), 72(6), 1962-1979

