$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Cyclized Products 14-22.
2-[5'-O-(tert-Butyldiphenylsilyl)-2',3'-O-isopropylidene-r-D-ribofuranosyl-1']-1-(N,N-dimethylsulfamoyl)indole
(14aα). By the typical procedure of the Mitsunobu reaction, 10aS (155 mg,
0.23 mmol) and PPh3 (1.5 equiv, 93 mg) were dissolved in THF and the
mixture was refluxed. Diethylazodicarboxylate (1.5 equiv, 50 mL) was then
added dropwise to the refluxing mixture, and heating was continued for 1
h. The solvent was evaporated to give a residual oil, which was
chromatographed on a silica gel column using 5% of ethyl acetate in
heptane to give 14aα (123 mg, 85%) as a white foam. Rf= 0.46 (7:3
heptane/ethyl acetate). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 1.11 (s, 9H), 1.24 (s, 3H),
1.26 (s, 3H), 2.73 (s, 6H), 3.75 (dd, 1H, J = 3.2 and 11.2 Hz), 3.92 (dd,
1H, J = 3.4 and 11.2 Hz), 4.35 (m, 1H), 4.94 (d, 1H, J = 6.0 Hz), 5.25
(t, 1H, J = 3.2 Hz), 5.84 (d, 1H, J = 4.2 Hz), 6.87 (s, 1H), 7.30 (m,
2H), 7.40 (m, 7H), 7.53 (m, 1H), 7.67 (m, 3H), 7.90 (m, 1H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3): δ 19.30, 25.13, 26.12, 27.01, 38.38, 66.05, 80.57, 82.90, 83.48,
83.85, 108.93, 112.47, 114.41, 120.78, 122.95, 123.63, 127.95, 129.22,
129.93, 130.05, 133.02, 135.60, 135.73, 137.07, 138.83. MS (ES): m/z 657
[M + Na]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, key step
