$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of 2-phenylethanol (1 mmol) in
THF (3 mL) was added successively methyl 4-hydroxy-benzoate (1.2 mmol)
and DPPBE (1.3 mmol, 0.5 M/THF). A solution of DIAD (1.3 mmol) in THF
(0.5 mL) was added drop wise over 15 min at r.t. and the progress of the
reaction was monitored by TLC. 4-Phenethyloxy-benzoic Acid Methyl Ester,
yield 84%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 3.06 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2 H), 3.81
(s, 3 H), 4.28 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2 H), 7.06 (d, J = 9 Hz, 2 H), 7.34- 7.21
(m, 5 H), 7.90 (d, J = 9 Hz, 2 H). MS (ES): m/z = 257 [MH]+. 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 165.8, 162.2, 138.0, 131.2, 128.9, 128.3, 126.3, 121.8,
114.4, 68.4, 51.7, 34.7. HRMS (FAB) calcd for C16H16O3 [M - H+]+:
256.109945. Found: 256.109963.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
